<p>This morning I went to a Discord<sup id="fnref:1"><a href="#fn:1" class="footnote-ref" role="doc-noteref">1</a></sup> server I haven&rsquo;t been to in probably over a year. They added a gaming channel (or maybe it was always there, I&rsquo;m not sure), and someone was talking about their issues playing scary games, so I chimed in. My main problem with these games is that they stress me out (that&rsquo;s kind of the point, right?), and I wanted to add my own list of horror games I want to get back to.</p>
<p>As I was looking at my list of games I included, I wanted to write a few lines about my more recent games in general — Just to keep track of what I&rsquo;m playing, what I played, and what I want to get back to. Steam allows that, to an extent, but <a href="https://taonaw.com/2023/11/17/sorry-for-littering.html">I know a better place: Backloggd</a>.</p>
<p>I had it integrated into my blog before, but its RSS feed is not reliable enough to count on and it doesn&rsquo;t always go through. Still, it&rsquo;s a good site, the only one of its kind I know. It contains the option to write a game &ldquo;journal&rdquo; as you go along, and because it&rsquo;s <em>not</em> Emacs, it motivated me to write only a quick comment and get the hell out of there before getting flashing-ads-in-your-face outrage (that&rsquo;s just how it is out there I guess).</p>
<p>I managed to <a href="https://backloggd.com/u/JTR/">write briefly about two games I&rsquo;m currently playing</a>, and I&rsquo;m happy about that. Writing about games is a struggle, and I&rsquo;d take anything that helps, even if it&rsquo;s an annoying flashing ad for a few seconds. Oh, and in case you&rsquo;re wondering, here&rsquo;s the list of horror (or horror-ish) games I want to get back into:</p>
<ul>
<li>Dredge</li>
<li>Signalis</li>
<li>Fran Bow</li>
<li>The Beast Inside</li>
<li>Still Wakes the Deep</li>
<li>Duskers</li>
</ul>
